---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ThisGHLGuy | ThisGHLGuy"
  description="Learn about ThisGHLGuy — the person behind the site, why it was built, and the mission to help agency owners and SaaS builders get the most out of GoHighLevel."
  canonical="/about/"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-700 to-brand-500 text-white py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <img
        src="/thisghlguy-logo.png"
        alt="ThisGHLGuy"
        width="120"
        height="120"
        class="h-28 w-28 object-contain mx-auto mb-6"
      />
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold mb-4" style="font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;">
        About ThisGHLGuy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-blue-100 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        The #1 independent resource for GoHighLevel users — built by someone who actually uses it every day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content -->
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">

    <div class="prose prose-lg prose-gray max-w-none">

      <h2>Why This Site Exists</h2>
      <p>
        GoHighLevel is one of the most powerful platforms for agencies and SaaS businesses — but it also has one of the steepest learning curves in the industry. When I started using it, I spent hours digging through YouTube videos, outdated forum posts, and vague documentation just to answer basic questions.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>ThisGHLGuy was built to fix that.</strong> Every guide, review, and tutorial here is written by someone who has actually set up GHL accounts, built automations, launched SaaS sub-accounts, and tested the features firsthand.
      </p>

      <h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Honest reviews</strong> — no hype, just real assessments of what GHL does well and where it falls short</li>
        <li><strong>Step-by-step tutorials</strong> — from first login all the way to advanced SaaS mode setup</li>
        <li><strong>Feature deep-dives</strong> — CRM, funnels, email marketing, SMS, pipelines, calendars, and more</li>
        <li><strong>Comparisons</strong> — how GoHighLevel stacks up against ClickFunnels, HubSpot, ActiveCampaign, and others</li>
        <li><strong>Automation guides</strong> — workflows, triggers, and sequences that save you hours every week</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who This Is For</h2>
      <p>
        This site is built for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Agency owners evaluating or already using GoHighLevel</li>
        <li>Marketers looking to get more out of their GHL subscription</li>
        <li>SaaS builders setting up white-label platforms for their clients</li>
        <li>Freelancers and consultants managing multiple client accounts</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Affiliate Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        ThisGHLGuy.com participates in the GoHighLevel affiliate program. If you sign up through a link on this site, I may earn a commission — at no extra cost to you. This helps keep the site free and ad-light.
      </p>
      <p>
        That said, every opinion on this site is my own. I only recommend GoHighLevel because I genuinely use it and believe it's the best all-in-one platform for agencies. I'll tell you when something is frustrating or not worth it.
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="mt-12 p-8 bg-brand-50 border border-brand-200 rounded-2xl text-center">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2" style="font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;">
        Ready to Try GoHighLevel?
      </h3>
      <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
        Start a free 14-day trial and see why thousands of agencies are building their entire business on GHL.
      </p>
      <a
        href="https://www.gohighlevel.com/?fp_ref=thisghlguy"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-brand-600 text-white font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-brand-700 transition-colors"
      >
        Try GoHighLevel Free →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
